            <ArticleTitle>Priming of Azabicycle Biosynthesis in the Azinomycin Class of Antitumor Agents.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>805-808</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.biochem.6b01108</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The biosynthesis of the azabicyclic ring system of the azinomycin family of antitumor agents represents the &quot;crown jewel&quot; of the pathway and is a complex process involving at least 14 enzymatic steps. This study reports on the first biosynthetic step, the inroads, in the construction of the novel aziridino [1,2-a]pyrrolidine, azabicyclic core, allowing us to support a new mechanism for azabicycle formation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
